.TH FREQUENCY_6022 1 "April 2026" "hantek6022api 2.10.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
frequency_6022 \- set calibration output frequency of Hantek 6022BE/BL oscilloscope
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frequency_6022
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-e\fR] [\fB\-\-min\fR | \fB\-\-max\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITIME\fR]
.I FREQ
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the calibration output frequency on the front panel GND/probe calibration
output of a Hantek 6022BE/BL oscilloscope. The firmware accepts only specific
discrete values between 32 Hz and 100 kHz.
.P
A value between two steps is rounded to the nearest representable frequency
with a warning on stderr; \fB\-\-min\fR sets the smallest representable
frequency >= \fIFREQ\fR (round up), \fB\-\-max\fR the largest one <= \fIFREQ\fR
(round down); \fB\-\-exact\fR rejects such values outright.
.P
After the frequency is set the program keeps its USB connection to the scope
open: until \fB\-t\fR seconds have passed, or (without \fB\-t\fR) until it is
interrupted with ^C. As long as the connection is open the USB port stays
active and the calibration output keeps running. Without this the kernel would
autosuspend the idle port shortly after the last access, which parks the FX2
CPU and freezes the software generated output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-exact\fR
Fail if \fIFREQ\fR is not representable instead of rounding it to the
nearest supported frequency.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\fR
Set the smallest supported frequency that is >= \fIFREQ\fR
(round non-representable values up, e.g. 433 Hz -> 440 Hz).
.TP
\fB\-\-max\fR
Set the largest supported frequency that is <= \fIFREQ\fR
(round non-representable values down, e.g. 433 Hz -> 430 Hz).
.TP
\fB\-t\fR \fITIME\fR, \fB\-\-time\fR \fITIME\fR
Hold the USB connection open for TIME seconds after setting the frequency;
without this option it is held until the program is interrupted with ^C.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIFREQ\fR
Calibration frequency in Hz (32 ... 100000).
.P
Supported steps:
.IP \(bu 4
32 Hz
.IP \(bu 4
40...990 Hz in 10 Hz steps
.IP \(bu 4
100...5500 Hz in 100 Hz steps
.IP \(bu 4
1000...100000 Hz in 1000 Hz steps
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR calibrate_6022 (1),
.BR capture_6022 (1),
.BR get_serial_number_6022 (1),
.BR upload_firmware_6022 (1)
